\DOC NONOVERLAPPING_TAC

\TYPE {NONOVERLAPPING_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves a goal whose conclusion asserts that two address ranges do not overlap,
closing it outright.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The conclusion {t} may be a non-overlap claim about two
memory regions stated either in the {nonoverlapping} form or in the explicit
modulo form, with region bases built from program counters, stack pointers,
word offsets and symbolic pointers, and with sizes that may be arithmetic
expressions in free variables. The assumptions {A} are left untouched and serve
as the source of the non-overlap and size facts from which the conclusion is
derived.
{
   A ?- t
   =============  NONOVERLAPPING_TAC
   (no goals)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the goal conclusion is a non-overlap assertion and the
goal is always closed, so no other behaviour is demonstrated.

\ENDDOC
